    ]
  },
  "inputs": [
    "instrument_map.csv",
    "session_soh.log"
  ],
  "row_order": "orders sorted by order_key; events sorted by (order_key, event_seq)",
  "compare_ignore_columns": [
    "raw"
  ],
  "edge_cases": [
    "fix_soh",
    "checksum_bodylength",
    "session_messages_skipped",
    "partial_fill",
    "replace_qty_down",
    "replace_price_new_order_id",
    "trade_bust_H",
    "trade_correct_G",
    "cancel_ack",
    "cancel_reject_35_9",
    "post_only_reject_18_6",
    "ioc_expire_C",
    "restate_D",
    "done_for_day_3",
    "order_key_from_clordid",
    "pending_states_dropped",
    "maker_taker_851"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Order-entry session log (outbound 35=D/F/G + inbound 35=8/9) plus session messages (35=A logon, 35=0 heartbeat) that must be skipped. A pure drop-copy session has only inbound 35=8 and no *_sent rows.",
    "BodyLength(9)/CheckSum(10) are correct for the SOH bytes. In the '|' file the checksum still refers to the SOH form, so pipe logs must not be checksum-validated.",
    "Pending states 150=A (pending new), E (pending replace), 6 (pending cancel) have no canonical event: dropped.",
    "150=5 replace: amend_keeps_priority null (FIX does not say; Coinbase Exchange FIX documents 'priority lost if qty increased or price modified, kept when qty decreased', but that is venue-specific). 5.7.2 then treats the qty-down amend of order 1 as a new leg unless the importer knows the venue rule (SPEC gap).",
    "150=H bust and 150=G correct reference the original ExecID via 19. Correct row: qty/px = corrected LastQty/LastPx; cum_qty taken from tag 14 (FIX says CumQty/LeavesQty/AvgPx reflect the order as of the correction).",
    "TransactTime(60): match_time on 150=F fills, gateway_time otherwise (SPEC). the importer also tags H/G corrections gateway_time: the 60 there is the correction time, not the match time.",
    "Inbound SendingTime(52) is the venue's clock and is NOT used as ts_local_recv (SPEC wording 'local times from SendingTime 52' is only valid for outbound messages: SPEC gap).",
    "Order 2 is rejected before an OrderID exists (37=NONE): order_key falls back to the root ClOrdID. Post-only is ExecInst 18=6 'Participate don't initiate'; there is no standard OrdRejReason for 'would cross', so the importer maps 150=8 on an 18=6 order to post_only_reject only when 58 mentions post only (SPEC gap).",
    "Order 3: IOC remainder reported as 150=C -> expire. Order 4: 35=9 OrderCancelReject (434=1) -> cancel_reject (SPEC table lists only 35=8 inbound); 150=D restate with 378=3 -> restate (px = new 44); 150=3 done for day -> done.",
    "Order 5: the venue assigns a new OrderID (OID-5b) on replace; order_key keeps the first OrderID and the chain is followed via 11/41. venue_order_id keeps OID-5 (schema has a single venue_order_id: SPEC gap).",
    "Fees from CommissionData 12/13=3/479; 851 1 -> maker, 2 -> taker.",
    "Tags 59: 0 -> day, 1 -> gtc, 3 -> ioc; orders with 18=6 -> tif post_only, post_only true.",
    "instrument_map.csv maps ACME to instrument_id 201, price_exp -4, size_exp 0.",
    "No log-line timestamps: ts_local_send = outbound SendingTime(52) at ms precision; inbound rows have ts_local_recv null.",
    "One message per line, raw SOH (0x01) delimiters, trailing newline after 10=xxx<SOH>."
  ],
